// Title: Uninstall Sysinternals Sysmon
// Sigma ID: 6a5f68d1-c4b5-46b9-94ee-5324892ea939
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-01-12 | Modified: 2026-06-29
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects the removal of Sysmon, which could be a potential attempt at defense evasion
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrators might use this command to remove Sysmon for debugging purposes
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1562.001/T1562.001.md#atomic-test-11---uninstall-sysmon
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sysinternals_sysmon_uninstall.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\Sysmon64.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\Sysmon64a.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\Sysmon.exe") or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "System activity monitor") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-u" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/u" or ProcessCommandLine contains "–u" or ProcessCommandLine contains "—u" or ProcessCommandLine contains "―u")
